# The credentials a session runs with. Never committed, and named here rather
# than left to habit: this repository is PUBLIC, and it is the one repository
# on this account where a slip would be visible to everybody immediately.
.env
.env.*

# What the wake fetches from the manager each session. It is not source: it is
# re-fetched every time, it goes stale the moment the manager changes, and
# behavior.json carries this agent's own instructions and the brief written for
# it. Named here for the same reason as the line above -- this repository is
# public, and one `git add -A` puts all of that in a history that cannot be
# taken back.
.kit/
